=== BEGIN Pages/Stock/Interface.purs ===

%file /home/bismuth/git/cheeblr/frontend/src/Pages/Stock/Interface.purs
%mod Pages.Stock.Interface

%uses Prelude
%uses API.Request as Request
%uses API.Stock as API
%uses Data.Array
%uses Data.Either
%uses Data.Foldable
%uses Data.Maybe
%uses Data.Tuple.Nested
%uses Deku.Control
%uses Deku.Core
%uses Deku.DOM as D
%uses Deku.DOM.Attributes as DA
%uses Deku.DOM.Listeners as DL
%uses Deku.Do as Deku
%uses Deku.Hooks
%uses Effect
%uses Effect.Aff
%uses Effect.Class
%uses Effect.Ref as Ref
%uses Effect.Unsafe
%uses Pages.Admin.Components.SSEStatus
%uses Pages.Stock.Components.AlertBanner
%uses Pages.Stock.Components.MessageThread
%uses Pages.Stock.Components.PullCard
%uses Types.Stock
%uses Types.UUID
%uses UI.Leave
%uses UI.Remote
%uses Utils.Audio
%uses Utils.SSE
%uses Config.Entity
%uses Types.Location

%untested useRef, page

useRef :: forall a. a -> (Ref.Ref a -> Nut) -> Nut
  ! unsafePerformEffect-based Ref creation; safe because Ref.new is idempotent and the Ref is captured in the continuation's closure.
  ! Workaround for not having a useRef hook in Deku; revisit if Deku adds one.
  ~ called by: Pages.Stock.Interface.page

page :: OnLeave -> Nut
  ! Loads the queue and opens the stream from UI.Remote.onMount.
  ! The stream is API.Stock.queueStreamUrl with the session cookie as the credential. Its close action is registered with onLeave.
  ! Request errors are shown in the status bar with the backend's text.
  ~ called by: Main.main

%decision SSEPushTriggersFullQueueReload
  what:    The SSE stream from /stock/queue/stream is used purely as a 'queue changed' notification; the handler ignores the event payload and calls loadQueue to refetch
  why:     Avoids encoding the full PullRequest type in the SSE event format; the REST endpoint is the source of truth. Trades extra HTTP requests for simpler protocol and avoids drift between SSE event shape and REST response shape. Cost: one extra round-trip per queue change; acceptable because changes are infrequent (human-initiated).
  affects: page

%decision NewPullDetectionViaPrevQueueDiff
  what:    New pull requests are detected by diffing prevQueueRef against the new fetch result rather than from a 'created' event type
  why:     The SSE event payload is ignored (see SSEPushTriggersFullQueueReload), so we can't tell from the event whether it was a create or an update. Diffing by prId catches creates without needing event-type discrimination. Side effect: only triggers audio + browser notification + alert banner for new pulls, not for status updates. Edits to existing pulls are silent. If the prev queue is empty (initial load), no notifications fire even if pulls are present; this is intentional to avoid spamming the user on app start.
  affects: page

%open_issue StreamAuthNotConfirmedInABrowser
  what:     The queue stream relies on the backend's CORS answer allowing credentials for an EventSource; this has been checked only against a mock
  why:      Utils.SSE opens the EventSource with withCredentials. The backend's reflectOriginMiddleware adds Access-Control-Allow-Origin and Allow-Credentials to every response, read from source. If the stream badge stays on Reconnecting against the real backend, look here first.
  affects:  page


