  ~ no callers in scanned roots

%decision WhenCapableUsesGuardForReactiveGating
  what:    whenCapable wraps children in Deku.Hooks.guard so the children are only mounted (not just hidden) when the capability is true
  why:     guard fully unmounts vs hides; this avoids hidden but mounted children running event handlers or holding refs. Means capability changes during a session (e.g. role downgrade) immediately remove the gated UI. Cost: re-mounting on cap toggle drops any component-local state. For most caps this is fine because they don't toggle mid-session.
  affects: whenCapable, withFallback

%open_issue DisabledUnlessIsNoOp
  what:     disabledUnless ignores both arguments and returns children unchanged
  why:      Probably intended to add a 'disabled' attribute to children based on capability, but the implementation is a passthrough. Currently no callers, so this hasn't caused visible problems, but the name lies about what it does. Either implement properly (would need to know how to attribute-mutate Nuts) or delete the function.
  affects:  disabledUnless

%open_issue ModuleHasNoUser
  what:     Nothing in the app imports this module
  why:      Route.nav and the pages read capabilities from the session record directly. Keep it only if reactive gating inside a page is wanted later.
  affects:  whenCapable


